  "details": "Avatar creators who have consistently uploaded a substantial amount of great content, have avatars with a high number of favorites, and didn't receive many reports or blocks, should have the opportunity to get their avatars verified. Verified avatars would be recognized as non-crasher avatars, which are safer to use. This verification would encourage more users to display these avatars and enable custom features like shaders, lights, particles, and animations through the safety system for these verified avatars.\n\nWhile this might make smaller avatar creators less noticeable, but it would improve the overall experience by ensuring that most users are using safe avatars. This system could also help filter out the small percentage of players who tend to use annoying, disturbing, nsfw, or crasher avatars, making VRChat a more enjoyable environment for everyone.\n\nBut even if that's not possible, it would be great to make it work locally, where people could mark some content creators or avatars verified by yourself, so you wouldn't need to manually click on \"Show Avatar\" every time when 2 or more people use the same avatar.",
